WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.882
Man:
U.S. Military escort cdc team.

2
00:00:16.884 --> 00:00:20.119
Requesting permission
to enter egyptian airspace.

3
00:00:20.121 --> 00:00:22.421
Man ♪2: Permission granted.

4
00:00:22.423 --> 00:00:24.957
Dr. Scott. on to the right.
Take a look.

5
00:00:24.959 --> 00:00:26.425
Man ♪3: He's on approach.

6
00:00:26.427 --> 00:00:29.862
Visibility... good.
Time to target... three minutes.

7
00:00:29.864 --> 00:00:31.096
Roger that. 2-2-0.

8
00:00:31.098 --> 00:00:32.398
Roger that. I see it.

9
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.533
Status... green.

10
00:00:34.535 --> 00:00:38.237
Dr. Scott. prepare for landing.

11
00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:42.141
Putting down close to...
20 feet.

12
00:00:42.143 --> 00:00:44.643
10 feet.

13
00:00:44.645 --> 00:00:47.479
And we're down.

14
00:00:47.481 --> 00:00:49.114
Doctor. you've got five minutes.

15
00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.089
This way.

16
00:00:57.091 --> 00:01:00.492
There are 6.000 quarantined
in this camp.

17
00:01:00.494 --> 00:01:01.894
We have 387 dead.

18
00:01:01.896 --> 00:01:03.395
My staff is down to six!

19
00:01:03.397 --> 00:01:05.397
I thought you were bringing
more doctors with you.

20
00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:14.206
These are the latest
to come down with the virus.

21
00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:17.009
Once the spots come.
they die in two days.

22
00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.172
I'm sorry.

23
00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:14.366
Slattery: Make sure those snowmobiles
go to starboard hangar "f"!

24
00:02:14.368 --> 00:02:17.569
Chief spurling. chief lewis. we
are getting under way at 1300.

25
00:02:17.571 --> 00:02:19.071
Let's pick up the pace. okay?!

26
00:02:19.073 --> 00:02:21.673
Yeah. I know all about
the naval mountain warfare unit.

27
00:02:21.675 --> 00:02:24.576
But I've never heard of a dog
setting foot on a destroyer.

28
00:02:24.578 --> 00:02:26.845
This isn't just a dog.
This is admiral halsey.

29
00:02:26.847 --> 00:02:28.313
And he's a mean operator.

30
00:02:28.315 --> 00:02:29.815
Yeah? Well. so is the captain.

31
00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.834
Rachel: You can just
put that down over there.

32
00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:54.006
Be careful.
That's delicate equipment.

33
00:02:54.008 --> 00:02:56.475
I take it
you're my new houseguest.

34
00:02:56.477 --> 00:02:58.844
I'm commander chandler.
ship's captain.

35
00:02:58.846 --> 00:03:00.612
Rachel scott.

36
00:03:00.614 --> 00:03:02.548
I'm sorry we had to take over
your helicopter bay.

37
00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.990
But it was the only space large
enough to accommodate our lab.

38
00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.388
I got 217 men and women
on this ship.

39
00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.857
Anything
I should be concerned about?

40
00:03:11.859 --> 00:03:13.525
Oh. this?

41
00:03:13.527 --> 00:03:16.061
Um. this is just so
we don't contaminate the work...

42
00:03:16.063 --> 00:03:19.464
Not the other way around.

43
00:03:19.466 --> 00:03:22.367
What exactly are you gonna
be studying up there?

44
00:03:22.369 --> 00:03:23.368
Birds.

45
00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.770
Birds?

46
00:03:24.772 --> 00:03:27.506
We are virologists...

47
00:03:27.508 --> 00:03:30.642
Tracking obscure microbes
in hard-to-get-to places.

48
00:03:30.644 --> 00:03:32.945
Pretty boring stuff. actually.

49
00:03:32.947 --> 00:03:37.082
We really do appreciate your
assistance. captain chandler.

50
00:03:37.084 --> 00:03:39.518
We're here to serve.

51
00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.154
Welcome aboard. doctor.

52
00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.653
Jeter: Roger that. Red deck.

53
00:04:14.655 --> 00:04:17.422
Bird's chocked and chained.
heading to the barn.

54
00:04:17.424 --> 00:04:19.558
Damn. it's cold.
I can't feel my face.

55
00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.159
Lieutenant granderson.
tell me...

56
00:04:21.161 --> 00:04:22.494
Do I still have my face?

57
00:04:22.496 --> 00:04:23.996
Yes. sir. though it looks like.

58
00:04:23.998 --> 00:04:25.831
You could use some lip balm.
sir.

59
00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:27.833
Should've taken
that desk job in miami.

60
00:04:27.835 --> 00:04:29.968
It is cold!

61
00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.986
Alisha: Captain's on the bridge!

62
00:04:47.988 --> 00:04:49.988
X.O. Slattery.

63
00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:53.125
Let's see if we can get
your frozen ass back to norfolk.

64
00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.595
T.A.O.. bridge. Bridge. t.A.O.

65
00:04:56.597 --> 00:04:59.464
Our helo just dropped a target
for our final missile test.

66
00:04:59.466 --> 00:05:01.867
Target's five feet long.
two feet wide.

67
00:05:01.869 --> 00:05:04.736
And in the icy water
has no heat signature.

68
00:05:04.738 --> 00:05:06.471
Let's find it and kill it.

69
00:05:06.473 --> 00:05:08.140
Woman: Scanning for target.

70
00:05:08.142 --> 00:05:09.141
Scanning zone.

71
00:05:09.143 --> 00:05:10.976
Man: Kill track 5205.

72
00:05:10.978 --> 00:05:13.078
Target acquired.
Target acquired. Break.

73
00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.547
Kill track 0845. aye.

74
00:05:15.549 --> 00:05:17.616
Mss. kill track 0845.

75
00:05:17.618 --> 00:05:18.984
Man: Missile ready to fire.

76
00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.754
Missile clear. 2-2-0. 30.

77
00:05:22.756 --> 00:05:24.823
30.000.

78
00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.102
Boom. Siegle: Target
confirmed kill.

79
00:05:37.104 --> 00:05:40.772
Good afternoon.<i> nathan james.</i>
This is the captain.

80
00:05:40.774 --> 00:05:43.909
After four very challenging
months at the top of the world.

81
00:05:43.911 --> 00:05:46.044
We have just passed
our final test.

82
00:05:46.046 --> 00:05:48.246
And I'm proud to say
you did it with flying colors.

83
00:05:48.248 --> 00:05:51.183
I'm asking the pentagon if
we can break radio silence today.

84
00:05:51.185 --> 00:05:53.752
And make calls and e-mail.

85
00:05:53.754 --> 00:05:56.021
Bravo zulu
to each and every one of you.

86
00:05:56.023 --> 00:05:59.057
Enjoy your success.
'cause we're going home.

87
00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.902
Gonna drop to 50 below.
Get them off the ice.

88
00:06:10.904 --> 00:06:12.304
Jeter: Aye. sir.

89
00:06:12.306 --> 00:06:15.207
Man: Dr. Scott. come in.

90
00:06:15.209 --> 00:06:16.908
Dr. Scott. are you there?

91
00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.210
Please respond.

92
00:06:18.212 --> 00:06:20.078
Dr. Scott. come in.

93
00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:29.054
You have got to be kidding me.

94
00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:32.891
We're so close.
We need to make sure.

95
00:06:32.893 --> 00:06:35.694
The isolate isn't contaminated.
We need more samples.

96
00:06:35.696 --> 00:06:37.963
It's all right. rachel.
We can come back tomorrow.

97
00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.634
Ma'am. we've been
trying to reach you.

98
00:06:42.636 --> 00:06:44.770
C.O. Wants you back on the ship.

99
00:06:44.772 --> 00:06:48.173
You can tell the captain
that I'll return when I'm ready.

100
00:06:48.175 --> 00:06:50.108
It wasn't an invitation. ma'am.

101
00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:53.945
Right now. Captain's orders.

102
00:06:53.947 --> 00:06:57.082
Man: Landing check is complete.
Gear down and locked.

103
00:06:57.084 --> 00:06:59.117
20 feet.

104
00:06:59.119 --> 00:07:01.720
10 feet.

105
00:07:01.722 --> 00:07:03.188
Wheels down.

106
00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:12.230
We haul ass from here. we can
make it back for the series.

107
00:07:12.232 --> 00:07:14.199
You don't really think
the cubs are still in it.

108
00:07:14.201 --> 00:07:16.268
It's the weakest division
in baseball.

109
00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:18.069
We were six games up
when we left.

110
00:07:18.071 --> 00:07:20.138
Yeah. that was June.
And they're the cubs.

111
00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:24.876
Captain chandler. you had no
right to pull me from my work.

112
00:07:24.878 --> 00:07:26.878
I'm gonna go check on the.
uh... Yeah.

113
00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.247
Those men are here
to support me.

114
00:07:29.249 --> 00:07:32.617
You don't send them to bring me in.
Those men are sailors in the u.S. Navy.

115
00:07:32.619 --> 00:07:34.286
And report directly to me. I
say when I am done and ready.

116
00:07:34.288 --> 00:07:35.887
My work is vital here.
and I have finally found.

117
00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:37.322
What I'm looking for! Doctor!

118
00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:41.159
First of all.
thanks for checking in.

119
00:07:41.161 --> 00:07:43.962
Think this is the first time
you said more than three words.

120
00:07:43.964 --> 00:07:45.764
To me since we left norfolk.

121
00:07:45.766 --> 00:07:48.099
Well. I am sorry that
I haven't had you over for tea.

122
00:07:48.101 --> 00:07:49.901
You know. your attitude
was mildly charming.

123
00:07:49.903 --> 00:07:53.138
Back in June in virginia.
but up here. at 50 below.

124
00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:56.741
When none of us have talked
to our families in four months.

125
00:07:56.743 --> 00:07:58.043
Not so charming.

126
00:07:58.045 --> 00:07:59.377
Yeah. well. charm
wasn't exactly my pri...

127
00:07:59.379 --> 00:08:01.179
Still talking.

128
00:08:01.181 --> 00:08:03.782
Now. I think I've been
more than a gracious host...

129
00:08:03.784 --> 00:08:05.984
Taxied you and your assistant
around the islands here.

130
00:08:05.986 --> 00:08:07.652
So you could chase after
your ducks.

131
00:08:07.654 --> 00:08:09.754
Arctic terns.
You need to wrap it up.

132
00:08:09.756 --> 00:08:11.823
Our mission's done.
and we'll be heading back.

133
00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:16.027
I'll take a rain check
on the tea.

134
00:08:22.869 --> 00:08:24.135
Benzo. eat some fruit.

135
00:08:24.137 --> 00:08:25.971
Oh!

136
00:08:25.973 --> 00:08:27.873
Come on. mr. Chung. It's our
last night at the north pole.

137
00:08:27.875 --> 00:08:29.307
Look. I know
you've got big plans.

138
00:08:29.309 --> 00:08:31.176
But don't you ever get your head
out of that book?

139
00:08:31.178 --> 00:08:32.077
Nope.

140
00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:34.145
Okay.

141
00:08:37.984 --> 00:08:39.017
Lieutenant.

142
00:08:39.019 --> 00:08:40.252
Lieutenant.

143
00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:51.796
Danny. whoa.

144
00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:54.833
Don't do that.

145
00:08:54.835 --> 00:08:56.167
Do what?

146
00:08:56.169 --> 00:08:57.969
You know
what that smile does to me.

147
00:08:57.971 --> 00:08:59.371
All's fair in love and war.

148
00:08:59.373 --> 00:09:02.207
Yeah.

149
00:09:02.209 --> 00:09:05.477
Kara... We'll be
home soon enough.

150
00:09:22.295 --> 00:09:23.929
Rachel: Hello.
Are you reading me?

151
00:09:23.931 --> 00:09:25.931
Come in.

152
00:09:25.933 --> 00:09:27.399
No. I cannot wait.

153
00:09:27.401 --> 00:09:29.868
This is dr. Rachel scott.

154
00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.737
I need to speak to the national
security adviser right away.

155
00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:35.240
<i>You</i> don't understand.
My mission is being compromised.

156
00:09:35.242 --> 00:09:37.809
And I need more time
to collect samples.

157
00:09:37.811 --> 00:09:39.411
We have a noisy channel.
I repeat.

158
00:09:39.413 --> 00:09:43.114
Mission objectives achieved.
We are ready to come home. Over.

159
00:09:44.284 --> 00:09:46.151
Man:
That's a negative. commander.

160
00:09:46.153 --> 00:09:48.086
The mission has been extended.
Over.

161
00:09:48.088 --> 00:09:50.121
Extended? Why?

162
00:09:50.123 --> 00:09:51.756
Maintain radio silence
and current position.

163
00:09:51.758 --> 00:09:53.892
Until you receive
further instructions.

164
00:09:53.894 --> 00:09:57.095
Mason:
Transmission terminated. sir.

165
00:10:19.151 --> 00:10:21.186
The hell is that woman doing?

166
00:10:37.804 --> 00:10:40.472
Rachel: Quincy... I
think we've got it.

167
00:10:46.245 --> 00:10:47.912
Danny: Sorry. man.
Did I wake you?

168
00:10:49.181 --> 00:10:51.149
Doc told me to keep my distance.

169
00:10:51.151 --> 00:10:53.284
The admiral's
scaring off the birds.

170
00:10:53.286 --> 00:10:55.086
Sure it was the dog
and not your breath?

171
00:10:55.088 --> 00:10:56.521
Whatever.

172
00:10:56.523 --> 00:10:59.424
Man. we should've been
out of here days ago.

173
00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.467
What the... Mason:
Aircraft in position.

174
00:11:09.469 --> 00:11:12.170
Seven six
decimal three five north.

175
00:11:12.172 --> 00:11:14.305
Zero five nine
decimal five eight east...

176
00:11:14.307 --> 00:11:17.108
Captain. I have three...
make that five unknown aircraft.

177
00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:19.611
Approaching. range 24 nautical
miles. approximately 80 knots.

178
00:11:35.594 --> 00:11:37.996
Those are not ours. man.

179
00:11:37.998 --> 00:11:40.231
No. They're russian.

180
00:11:57.216 --> 00:11:58.416
Come on!

181
00:11:58.418 --> 00:12:00.485
Quincy.
we have to save the samples!

182
00:12:00.487 --> 00:12:02.120
Help me!
Leave the box! Let's go!

183
00:12:02.122 --> 00:12:04.956
Rachel. leave the box!

184
00:12:33.587 --> 00:12:35.487
Let's go! Right now!

185
00:12:39.059 --> 00:12:41.559
Let's go! Come on!

186
00:12:45.331 --> 00:12:47.599
Quincy!

187
00:13:08.621 --> 00:13:10.088
Drop.

188
00:13:11.358 --> 00:13:12.457
Aah!

189
00:13:21.233 --> 00:13:23.968
Set general quarters. General
quarters. general quarters.

190
00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:25.270
All hands.
man your battle stations.

191
00:13:25.272 --> 00:13:26.704
Transit up and forward
starboard side.

192
00:13:26.706 --> 00:13:27.705
Down and aft portside.

193
00:13:27.707 --> 00:13:30.074
Unknown aircraft...

194
00:13:30.076 --> 00:13:32.510
Man: T.A.O.. air.
New air contact 80234.

195
00:13:32.512 --> 00:13:35.046
At 015 at 36.000 yards.
Inbound...

196
00:13:35.048 --> 00:13:36.514
T.A.O..
surface manned and ready.

197
00:13:36.516 --> 00:13:38.416
Deploy scat.
Ciws to a.A.W. Auto.

198
00:13:38.418 --> 00:13:40.318
Hold fire on.

199
00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.359
Aah!

200
00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.637
Take him alive!

201
00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:04.474
All engines ahead flank! Hard left rudder!
All engines ahead flank. aye!

202
00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.281
Mason:
...United states naval warship.

203
00:14:10.283 --> 00:14:12.350
Identify yourself
and alter your course.

204
00:14:12.352 --> 00:14:15.253
Or you will be subject
to defensive actions. Over.

205
00:14:15.255 --> 00:14:16.554
Evaluate as inbound missile.

206
00:14:16.556 --> 00:14:18.556
Recommend launch chaff.
Brace for shock!

207
00:14:18.558 --> 00:14:20.191
All hands. brace for shock.

208
00:14:35.107 --> 00:14:37.709
Take 'em out.

209
00:14:48.387 --> 00:14:49.587
Go to the 5 inch!

210
00:14:49.589 --> 00:14:51.456
Surface. t.A.O..
kill track 5024.

211
00:14:51.458 --> 00:14:54.192
Kara: Surface. aye.
Guns. kill track 5024.

212
00:14:54.194 --> 00:14:55.560
Man: Guns. aye.

213
00:15:07.072 --> 00:15:08.740
You okay?!

214
00:15:08.742 --> 00:15:11.175
Clear! Come on.

215
00:15:19.451 --> 00:15:20.785
Chandler: Where's dr. Scott?!

216
00:15:20.787 --> 00:15:22.253
She's banged up pretty good.

217
00:15:22.255 --> 00:15:23.855
Doc's looking at her
in hangar two.

218
00:15:33.233 --> 00:15:36.134
What'd he say?

219
00:15:36.136 --> 00:15:37.869
"The cure."

220
00:15:39.538 --> 00:15:41.606
He wants the cure.

221
00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.881
All our guys are accounted for.
We at war with the russians?

222
00:15:49.883 --> 00:15:51.983
Get me fleet forces.
They don't answer. get me nmcc.

223
00:15:51.985 --> 00:15:53.551
They don't answer.
get me secdef.

224
00:15:53.553 --> 00:15:55.820
Supposed to be radio silent.
Not anymore.

225
00:15:57.756 --> 00:15:59.958
I told you I'm fine.
Just hurry up.

226
00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.693
Where's quincy?
I need my samples.

227
00:16:01.695 --> 00:16:02.994
You don't get your samples.

228
00:16:02.996 --> 00:16:05.830
Until you tell me
what's going on here.

229
00:16:05.832 --> 00:16:08.032
You have no authority
over me... everybody out!

230
00:16:08.034 --> 00:16:11.002
You need to hand that case
over to me right now.

231
00:16:11.004 --> 00:16:12.770
We may have just gone to war
with russia.

232
00:16:12.772 --> 00:16:14.372
And they were clearly after you.

233
00:16:14.374 --> 00:16:16.407
No more secrets.

234
00:16:16.409 --> 00:16:17.608
Tell me about the cure!

235
00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:19.911
I can't say anything.

236
00:16:19.913 --> 00:16:21.980
Until I speak to the national security... I
swear to god. I will throw this overboard!

237
00:16:21.982 --> 00:16:23.047
I want answers!

238
00:16:24.651 --> 00:16:26.651
You want answers?

239
00:16:30.723 --> 00:16:33.925
Seven months ago. outside cairo.
there was an outbreak...

240
00:16:33.927 --> 00:16:36.527
A virus of unknown origin.

241
00:16:36.529 --> 00:16:37.795
Its genetic structure.

242
00:16:37.797 --> 00:16:39.664
Was like nothing any of us
had ever seen.

243
00:16:39.666 --> 00:16:41.666
It swept throughout the village.

244
00:16:41.668 --> 00:16:44.836
Killing everyone
that it infected.

245
00:16:44.838 --> 00:16:46.738
Egyptian officials claimed
the outbreak was contained.

246
00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.006
But it wasn't.

247
00:16:48.008 --> 00:16:50.775
Instead. it continued
to mutate and spread.

248
00:16:50.777 --> 00:16:55.013
The cdc and the w.H.O.
Wanted to sample the virus.

249
00:16:55.015 --> 00:16:57.548
From the victims
to create a vaccine.

250
00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.984
But nothing worked.

251
00:16:59.986 --> 00:17:03.488
It was my belief that we needed
to find the primordial strain.

252
00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:04.622
Here in the arctic.

253
00:17:04.624 --> 00:17:06.758
The birds.

254
00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:09.494
They're just the carriers.

255
00:17:09.496 --> 00:17:11.996
They pick up the virus
from the melting permafrost.

256
00:17:11.998 --> 00:17:14.032
We finally found
their feeding ground.

257
00:17:14.034 --> 00:17:15.967
So you have what you need
to stop this thing?

258
00:17:15.969 --> 00:17:18.102
I won't know until we get it
back to the lab.

259
00:17:18.104 --> 00:17:20.104
We're running out of time.

260
00:17:20.106 --> 00:17:21.839
The virus back home
is moving quicker.

261
00:17:21.841 --> 00:17:23.441
Than any of us
could've imagined.

262
00:17:23.443 --> 00:17:24.876
How would you know that?

263
00:17:24.878 --> 00:17:27.078
We've been radio silent
since we left norfolk.

264
00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:29.714
Because I have my own sat phone.

265
00:17:29.716 --> 00:17:33.684
We were at emcon so no one
would know our position!

266
00:17:33.686 --> 00:17:36.754
We were at emcon
to protect<i> my</i> mission...

267
00:17:36.756 --> 00:17:38.823
Not yours.

268
00:17:38.825 --> 00:17:40.925
Orders came
from the white house.

269
00:17:40.927 --> 00:17:43.461
Well. you led the russians
right to us.

270
00:17:43.463 --> 00:17:45.063
And endangered my entire crew.

271
00:17:45.065 --> 00:17:47.465
It was imperative
that I stay in contact.

272
00:17:47.467 --> 00:17:49.467
With the labs back home
to keep them informed.

273
00:17:49.469 --> 00:17:50.968
Of my progress.

274
00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:53.237
I don't think you understand
what we're talking about here.

275
00:17:53.239 --> 00:17:54.672
Enlighten me.

276
00:17:54.674 --> 00:17:55.807
When we left norfolk.

277
00:17:55.809 --> 00:17:59.210
The virus was at phase two.

278
00:17:59.212 --> 00:18:04.015
Limited to small clusters
in asia and africa.

279
00:18:04.017 --> 00:18:09.654
We are now at phase six...
Global pandemic.

280
00:18:10.956 --> 00:18:14.025
80% of the world's population
is infected.

281
00:18:15.928 --> 00:18:20.631
The world is sick.
captain chandler...

282
00:18:20.633 --> 00:18:22.033
Very sick.

283
00:18:22.035 --> 00:18:24.168
Are you telling me
the whole world is dying.

284
00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:26.070
And they send two people
to save it?

285
00:18:27.773 --> 00:18:31.175
It took weeks to convince the
government to even send me here.

286
00:18:33.011 --> 00:18:34.979
Most of my colleagues
think that I'm insane.

287
00:18:34.981 --> 00:18:36.047
Are you?

288
00:18:36.049 --> 00:18:42.019
I told you... That
what's in that case...

289
00:18:42.021 --> 00:18:44.122
Might be the only hope
that we have.

290
00:18:44.124 --> 00:18:46.290
Captain. we have the president
of the United States.

291
00:18:46.292 --> 00:18:48.359
On the vidcom.

292
00:18:51.797 --> 00:18:54.799
I'm sorry
you had to find out this way.

293
00:18:59.204 --> 00:19:01.873
Can I have my samples now?

294
00:19:08.747 --> 00:19:10.815
Man: Stand by for the president.

295
00:19:10.817 --> 00:19:13.818
Morning. commander.

296
00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:15.286
Ma'am?

297
00:19:15.288 --> 00:19:17.688
I know. The last you heard.
I was speaker of the house.

298
00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:20.258
The president
died two months ago.

299
00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:22.960
The vice president a week later.

300
00:19:22.962 --> 00:19:24.929
What's left
of the federal government.

301
00:19:24.931 --> 00:19:27.064
Is holed up
200 feet below the white house.

302
00:19:27.066 --> 00:19:29.834
And communication
is getting spotty.

303
00:19:29.836 --> 00:19:32.803
So we need to know now...

304
00:19:32.805 --> 00:19:36.207
Does dr. Scott have what
she needs to make a vaccine?

305
00:19:36.209 --> 00:19:37.642
She thinks so. ma'am.

306
00:19:37.644 --> 00:19:39.243
We are sending you
the coordinates.

307
00:19:39.245 --> 00:19:43.114
To a secure bio-lab
on the coast of north carolina.

308
00:19:43.116 --> 00:19:45.983
Ma'am. we were just attacked
by the russians.

309
00:19:45.985 --> 00:19:48.986
Russia no longer has
a functioning government.

310
00:19:48.988 --> 00:19:50.621
From what we're hearing.

311
00:19:50.623 --> 00:19:53.858
A breakaway force is operating
on its own authority.

312
00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:56.594
We're trying to ascertain
all the facts.

313
00:19:56.596 --> 00:19:59.630
Ma'am. our families...
how do we find out if...

314
00:19:59.632 --> 00:20:01.866
I wish I could tell you.
captain.

315
00:20:01.868 --> 00:20:05.870
Most of our population.
al... with our armed forces.

316
00:20:05.872 --> 00:20:07.271
Is dying or dead.

317
00:20:07.273 --> 00:20:09.707
We have no allies.

318
00:20:09.709 --> 00:20:11.309
We have no enemies.

319
00:20:11.311 --> 00:20:14.712
Just a world of sick.
desperate people.

320
00:20:14.714 --> 00:20:17.381
Your ship was fortunate enough
to be out of the hot zone.

321
00:20:17.383 --> 00:20:18.883
These past months.

322
00:20:18.885 --> 00:20:21.619
If dr. Scott
has the makings of a cure.

323
00:20:21.621 --> 00:20:24.288
You have to come home... Now.

324
00:20:31.897 --> 00:20:34.031
Man:<i> Supply chains</i>
<i>are completely broken.</i>

325
00:20:34.033 --> 00:20:35.800
<i>Food is in short supply.</i>
<i>Hospitals...</i>

326
00:20:35.802 --> 00:20:37.235
Woman: <i>...Chinese government.</i>

327
00:20:37.237 --> 00:20:39.036
<i>Have detonated the bomb</i>
<i>on its own people.</i>

328
00:20:39.038 --> 00:20:40.905
<i>To stop the spread</i>
<i>of the deadly virus.</i>

329
00:20:40.907 --> 00:20:42.907
Woman ♪2:<i> With possibly</i>
<i>half the world's population</i>

330
00:20:42.909 --> 00:20:45.810
<i>Dead or dying. rumors that</i>
<i>the u.S. Is hoarding a vaccine.</i>

331
00:20:45.812 --> 00:20:47.645
<i>Continue to swirl.</i>

332
00:20:47.647 --> 00:20:49.180
Man ♪2:<i> Urban services</i>
<i>are completely overwhelmed.</i>

333
00:20:49.182 --> 00:20:51.649
<i>In most cities.</i>
<i>entire power grids are down.</i>

334
00:20:51.651 --> 00:20:53.651
<i>Making communication</i>
<i>next to impossible.</i>

335
00:20:53.653 --> 00:20:55.920
Man ♪3:<i> People are asking.</i>
<i>"where is the government?"</i>

336
00:20:55.922 --> 00:20:59.056
<i>The virus has no treatment.</i>
<i>no vaccine.</i>

337
00:20:59.058 --> 00:21:02.727
So this whole weapons test...
it was all just a cover.

338
00:21:06.198 --> 00:21:08.099
And emcon alpha...

339
00:21:08.101 --> 00:21:10.401
Keep us in the dark about
what was going on at home.

340
00:21:12.004 --> 00:21:15.072
There's an unmanned refueling
station off the coast of France.

341
00:21:15.074 --> 00:21:17.808
If we operate at trail shaft.
we should just make it.

342
00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:19.710
How do we know
they have enough fuel.

343
00:21:19.712 --> 00:21:21.212
To get us across the atlantic?

344
00:21:21.214 --> 00:21:22.747
We don't.

345
00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.218
What do we tell the crew?

346
00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:29.153
Everything.

347
00:21:30.956 --> 00:21:33.424
We tell them everything.

348
00:21:41.833 --> 00:21:42.800
Captain?

349
00:21:43.835 --> 00:21:45.136
Crew's assembled.

350
00:21:50.942 --> 00:21:53.277
Ship's company. attention!

351
00:22:07.726 --> 00:22:11.996
I have news... From home.

352
00:22:28.513 --> 00:22:29.947
Mason: Any station this net.

353
00:22:29.949 --> 00:22:32.016
This is<i> nathan james</i>
transmitting in the blind.

354
00:22:32.018 --> 00:22:34.885
On fleetsat one. two. and three.
over.

355
00:22:34.887 --> 00:22:35.986
Is anybody out there?

356
00:22:41.894 --> 00:22:43.794
<i>Due to widespread</i>
<i>system failure.</i>

357
00:22:43.796 --> 00:22:46.063
<i>The number you are calling</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

358
00:22:46.065 --> 00:22:47.932
<i>This message</i>
<i>will not be updated.</i>

359
00:22:51.070 --> 00:22:52.570
Daddy!

360
00:22:52.572 --> 00:22:54.105
Darien: I can't believe
I'm gonna go that long.

361
00:22:54.107 --> 00:22:55.606
Without hearing your voice.

362
00:22:58.176 --> 00:22:59.744
Ashley: We miss you. daddy.

363
00:23:11.923 --> 00:23:13.891
Captain's on the bridge!

364
00:23:15.927 --> 00:23:18.562
Sir. we're 50 miles
off the coast of europe.

365
00:23:18.564 --> 00:23:21.198
And still no contact
with french naval command.

366
00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:24.068
We've got extra watch
and guns at the ready.

367
00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:26.170
Were you able to reach home?

368
00:23:26.172 --> 00:23:28.105
No. sir.

369
00:23:28.107 --> 00:23:31.575
I think only four people
got through to anyone.

370
00:23:31.577 --> 00:23:34.712
And the news wasn't good.

371
00:23:34.714 --> 00:23:37.181
Last time we made port
in France.

372
00:23:37.183 --> 00:23:38.983
I promised my girlfriend.

373
00:23:38.985 --> 00:23:41.952
We'd come back
and see paris together.

374
00:23:43.955 --> 00:23:49.126
With everything. that's all
I keep thinking about.

375
00:23:49.128 --> 00:23:51.996
Well. that's the stuff
that matters.

376
00:23:55.300 --> 00:23:57.802
Jeter: X.O.'s on the bridge.

377
00:24:00.205 --> 00:24:02.373
I got through to home.

378
00:24:02.375 --> 00:24:06.076
My boy's gone.

379
00:24:06.078 --> 00:24:07.978
Oh. mike.

380
00:24:07.980 --> 00:24:12.283
Christine is up in deer park.
some sort of safe zone for now.

381
00:24:12.285 --> 00:24:14.018
Girls are with her.

382
00:24:14.020 --> 00:24:16.120
Why don't you take a break?
I-I got it. No. no.

383
00:24:16.122 --> 00:24:19.123
I'm not gonna sit around
my cabin staring at the walls.

384
00:24:19.125 --> 00:24:20.891
This is where I need to be.

385
00:24:20.893 --> 00:24:22.259
Sir. we have a fire order.

386
00:24:22.261 --> 00:24:23.994
It came across all channels.
but it's garbled.

387
00:24:23.996 --> 00:24:26.030
They cannot authenticate.

388
00:24:28.768 --> 00:24:31.168
Lieutenant? Siegle: Confirmed fire
order. sir. but the target's unclear.

389
00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:32.770
Vampire. vampire. vampire!

390
00:24:32.772 --> 00:24:34.271
Missile incoming high and fast.

391
00:24:34.273 --> 00:24:36.640
Spin four tomahawks.
Hold for a target location.

392
00:24:36.642 --> 00:24:38.242
These coordinates
don't make any sense.

393
00:24:38.244 --> 00:24:40.044
Mason: No response from command.
E.C.O.. aye. Break.

394
00:24:40.046 --> 00:24:41.412
Mml. align four echo missiles.

395
00:24:41.414 --> 00:24:42.980
And place them
in the reload pool.

396
00:24:42.982 --> 00:24:46.283
Do we have a target I.D.?
Now five-one and trail.

397
00:24:46.285 --> 00:24:48.953
Woman: Missile fired from a surface
ship in the north atlantic.

398
00:24:48.955 --> 00:24:52.723
Man: Ballistic missile traveling
at 9.700 miles per hour.

399
00:24:52.725 --> 00:24:54.191
Confirmed. We have
a nuclear burn in the air.

400
00:24:54.193 --> 00:24:56.193
We have no chance to intercept.

401
00:24:56.195 --> 00:24:57.428
Man: Batten down.

402
00:24:57.430 --> 00:24:59.730
Officer at the one.
seal the ship.

403
00:24:59.732 --> 00:25:01.665
Prepare for nuclear detonation.

404
00:25:01.667 --> 00:25:03.033
This is no drill.

405
00:25:03.035 --> 00:25:05.202
Sir. the missile overshot us.
Headed for land.

406
00:25:09.941 --> 00:25:11.976
Detonation in 12 seconds.

407
00:25:16.815 --> 00:25:18.282
Bridge. shield your eyes.

408
00:25:20.685 --> 00:25:22.353
God help us.

409
00:25:39.704 --> 00:25:43.941
Give me a status report on
the switchboard and generators.

410
00:25:43.943 --> 00:25:45.976
Who's that? Chung. sir.

411
00:25:45.978 --> 00:25:47.311
Anyone hurt? No. sir.

412
00:25:47.313 --> 00:25:48.979
What's our engine status?

413
00:25:48.981 --> 00:25:51.181
Sir. the. uh. electromagnetic
pulse from the bomb.

414
00:25:51.183 --> 00:25:52.416
Blew our grid.

415
00:25:52.418 --> 00:25:54.485
Engines won't spin.
No propulsion.

416
00:25:54.487 --> 00:25:56.387
Emergency lights operating
on battery power.

417
00:25:56.389 --> 00:25:57.388
Jeter: Captain!

418
00:25:57.390 --> 00:25:59.023
That you. master chief?

419
00:25:59.025 --> 00:26:00.858
Commo says the radios are down.

420
00:26:00.860 --> 00:26:02.726
No way to get messages
in or out.

421
00:26:02.728 --> 00:26:05.095
We need to move this ship
away from the blast zone.

422
00:26:05.097 --> 00:26:08.065
Lieutenant. let's get
those engines back online.

423
00:26:08.067 --> 00:26:09.266
Yes. sir.

424
00:26:10.869 --> 00:26:12.369
What temperature are we at?

425
00:26:12.371 --> 00:26:14.405
41 degrees. and we've lost
negative pressure.

426
00:26:14.407 --> 00:26:16.106
Damn it.
We're gonna lose everything.

427
00:26:16.108 --> 00:26:17.107
Okay. get the ice.

428
00:26:19.110 --> 00:26:20.411
Fuses in.

429
00:26:20.413 --> 00:26:22.413
Open valves three. four.
and five.

430
00:26:22.415 --> 00:26:25.149
Shut valve to auxiliary engines
and emergency air.

431
00:26:25.151 --> 00:26:26.350
Fuel lever on start.

432
00:26:26.352 --> 00:26:27.985
All right. Give it a kick start.

433
00:26:29.955 --> 00:26:32.523
Sir. we only have one more fuse.

434
00:26:32.525 --> 00:26:35.292
The jet stream's pushing
everything north-northeast.

435
00:26:35.294 --> 00:26:38.362
We got a cloud of radiation
about to drop right on us.

436
00:26:38.364 --> 00:26:39.830
Give it to me.

437
00:26:40.298 --> 00:26:41.832
Sir. it won't hold. It'll hold.

438
00:26:42.500 --> 00:26:45.102
Captain. let somebody else do this.
Rip it.

439
00:26:45.104 --> 00:26:46.437
Get your hand out of there.
You heard me.

440
00:26:46.439 --> 00:26:48.305
Captain. don't. I said rip it!

441
00:27:02.020 --> 00:27:04.488
Badass. captain.

442
00:27:04.490 --> 00:27:07.891
Badass.

443
00:27:09.894 --> 00:27:11.895
Alisha: All engines ahead full.
Left full rudder.

444
00:27:11.897 --> 00:27:13.297
Steady on new course 270.

445
00:27:13.299 --> 00:27:14.465
What's our fuel percentage?

446
00:27:14.467 --> 00:27:16.033
11%. sir.

447
00:27:16.035 --> 00:27:19.069
Even at max conserve.
we'll run dry in six hours.

448
00:27:19.071 --> 00:27:20.471
Any contacts on surface search?

449
00:27:20.473 --> 00:27:22.206
No. sir. 30-mile range.

450
00:27:22.208 --> 00:27:24.508
What is that in the radar shadow?
Change range scale.

451
00:27:24.510 --> 00:27:26.944
Looks like a ship.

452
00:27:26.946 --> 00:27:28.946
Calculate a course to intercept.

453
00:27:48.299 --> 00:27:50.934
Man: Markings indicate
the ship is italian.

454
00:27:50.936 --> 00:27:53.437
Bridge to bridge operational?

455
00:27:53.439 --> 00:27:55.072
I think so. sir.

456
00:27:57.242 --> 00:28:00.844
Vessel in vicinity 48 degrees
north. 15 degrees west.

457
00:28:00.846 --> 00:28:04.181
This is u.S. Navy warship 151
on your starboard bow.

458
00:28:04.183 --> 00:28:06.417
Acknowledge
and identify yourself. Over.

459
00:28:18.263 --> 00:28:21.098
Smith. rowler. benz. green.
you're on provisions.

460
00:28:21.100 --> 00:28:24.034
Master chief. you'll assist
chung with the unrep.

461
00:28:24.036 --> 00:28:27.071
We get as much food and fuel
as we can and we get out.

462
00:28:27.073 --> 00:28:28.972
Let's move.

463
00:28:28.974 --> 00:28:32.176
Rachel: Remember. if the ship
has been impacted by the virus.

464
00:28:32.178 --> 00:28:35.312
It's airborne
and highly. highly contagious.

465
00:28:35.314 --> 00:28:38.682
Even from
a recently deceased corpse.

466
00:28:38.684 --> 00:28:42.052
You must keep your helmets on
at all times.

467
00:28:42.054 --> 00:28:45.489
You trained for this.
You can do it.

468
00:28:47.125 --> 00:28:49.293
Chandler: Lieutenant. send
naval warfare to the kitchen.

469
00:28:49.295 --> 00:28:50.994
Get as much food and supplies
as you can.

470
00:28:50.996 --> 00:28:52.229
We got the stock rooms.

471
00:28:52.231 --> 00:28:53.864
Benzo and I will take
the starboard side.

472
00:28:53.866 --> 00:28:55.332
Make our way to the galley.

473
00:28:55.334 --> 00:28:56.934
Master chief. get that fuel line
across and pump it.

474
00:28:56.936 --> 00:28:58.135
Sending the pull line.

475
00:29:03.675 --> 00:29:06.343
Sending over the hose.

476
00:29:06.345 --> 00:29:08.445
Feed the line.

477
00:29:08.447 --> 00:29:09.947
Engineering. bridge.

478
00:29:09.949 --> 00:29:12.950
Engage fueling.

479
00:29:12.952 --> 00:29:15.152
System online! Commence fueling!

480
00:29:38.109 --> 00:29:39.376
Ship's clear.

481
00:29:39.378 --> 00:29:41.111
No one alive.
commander chandler. Over.

482
00:30:32.430 --> 00:30:35.933
Man: Aiutami.

483
00:30:35.935 --> 00:30:37.267
Aiutami.

484
00:30:37.269 --> 00:30:38.535
Dr. Scott!

485
00:30:40.071 --> 00:30:43.240
Aiutami.

486
00:30:57.422 --> 00:30:59.456
Aiutami.

487
00:30:59.458 --> 00:31:01.091
He wants help.

488
00:31:01.093 --> 00:31:03.360
The only thing that can
help him now is morphine.

489
00:31:09.968 --> 00:31:11.368
Let go.

490
00:31:11.370 --> 00:31:13.403
Let go.

491
00:31:30.188 --> 00:31:32.322
Oh. shit!

492
00:31:32.324 --> 00:31:33.323
Frankie!

493
00:31:37.962 --> 00:31:39.463
Put your mask on!

494
00:31:39.465 --> 00:31:40.631
No! It's off!

495
00:31:42.867 --> 00:31:44.534
Oh. shit.

496
00:31:52.844 --> 00:31:55.145
Frankie. Hey.

497
00:31:55.147 --> 00:31:59.082
Frankie! It's all right!

498
00:31:59.084 --> 00:32:00.984
Look! Get up!

499
00:32:00.986 --> 00:32:03.387
Get away. man. Get away!

500
00:32:05.290 --> 00:32:07.391
Master chief.
we're running dry here.

501
00:32:07.393 --> 00:32:09.126
Engineering. bridge. Disengage.

502
00:32:09.128 --> 00:32:11.094
Yes. sir.
They've got it. mr. Chung.

503
00:32:11.096 --> 00:32:12.963
Let's get out of here. Yes. sir.

504
00:32:12.965 --> 00:32:14.865
Danny: You're gonna be fine!
Frankie: Get away!

505
00:32:14.867 --> 00:32:17.501
Just take the food and go get
the hell out of here. No!

506
00:32:17.503 --> 00:32:20.103
I'm not leaving you. frankie!
I'm a dead man.

507
00:32:20.105 --> 00:32:21.438
Just get out of here.

508
00:32:21.440 --> 00:32:23.540
No. man. I'm not leaving you!

509
00:32:23.542 --> 00:32:25.542
You tell him.

510
00:32:27.545 --> 00:32:29.012
He's been exposed.

511
00:32:29.014 --> 00:32:30.314
We put him back in his suit.

512
00:32:30.316 --> 00:32:32.316
And we quarantine him
on the ship!

513
00:32:32.318 --> 00:32:35.452
You can't risk it. sir.
Mission comes first.

514
00:32:35.454 --> 00:32:38.422
I'm not all too interested
in dying like these people.

515
00:32:38.424 --> 00:32:39.923
Give me the gun. sailor.

516
00:32:39.925 --> 00:32:42.526
Frankie. don't be stupid.

517
00:32:42.528 --> 00:32:44.995
I am giving you a direct order!

518
00:32:44.997 --> 00:32:46.330
Put down that weapon!

519
00:32:46.332 --> 00:32:47.597
Frankie. no!

520
00:33:04.916 --> 00:33:08.285
Jeter: Lord god.
by the power of your word.

521
00:33:08.287 --> 00:33:12.022
You stilled the chaos
of the primeval seas.

522
00:33:12.024 --> 00:33:15.092
Made the raging waters
of the flood subside.

523
00:33:15.094 --> 00:33:18.028
And calmed the storm
on the sea of galilee.

524
00:33:18.030 --> 00:33:22.532
As we commit our brother
franklin edward benz to the sea.

525
00:33:22.534 --> 00:33:25.802
Grant him peace and tranquility.

526
00:33:25.804 --> 00:33:29.806
Until that day when franklin
and all those who believe in you.

527
00:33:29.808 --> 00:33:32.943
Will be raised
to the glory of new life.

528
00:33:32.945 --> 00:33:35.812
Promised in the waters
of baptism.

529
00:33:35.814 --> 00:33:36.913
Amen.

530
00:33:54.098 --> 00:33:56.867
Man: Left face!

531
00:33:56.869 --> 00:33:59.970
Present arms!

532
00:33:59.972 --> 00:34:01.004
Ready.

533
00:34:01.006 --> 00:34:02.606
Aim.

534
00:34:03.541 --> 00:34:05.976
Fire!

535
00:34:07.146 --> 00:34:08.545
Fire!

536
00:34:08.547 --> 00:34:09.579
Ready.

537
00:34:11.383 --> 00:34:13.617
Fire!

538
00:34:27.031 --> 00:34:29.499
These people depend on me.

539
00:34:29.501 --> 00:34:33.370
I'm in uncharted territory here.

540
00:34:33.372 --> 00:34:35.105
We all are.

541
00:34:35.107 --> 00:34:38.241
Not you. You saw this coming.

542
00:34:38.243 --> 00:34:40.010
I never thought
it would spread so fast.

543
00:34:42.413 --> 00:34:44.548
But now I know why it did.

544
00:34:44.550 --> 00:34:47.918
I compared the blood
that we took from the italian.

545
00:34:47.920 --> 00:34:50.387
To some samples I took
before we left.

546
00:34:50.389 --> 00:34:52.289
The virus has an extra gene now.

547
00:34:52.291 --> 00:34:55.292
Which could have only been added
with human intervention.

548
00:34:55.294 --> 00:34:57.227
So it was weaponized.

549
00:34:57.229 --> 00:34:58.562
Maybe.

550
00:34:58.564 --> 00:35:01.932
Or maybe it escaped
from a lab somehow.

551
00:35:01.934 --> 00:35:04.134
But I think I know
how to stop it.

552
00:35:04.136 --> 00:35:07.237
All the virus cares about
is replicating.

553
00:35:07.239 --> 00:35:10.440
The engineered version
lets it do that unchecked.

554
00:35:10.442 --> 00:35:12.676
So it no longer needs to mutate.

555
00:35:12.678 --> 00:35:17.414
Which makes it stable and easier
to defeat with a vaccine.

556
00:35:17.416 --> 00:35:19.583
Then why hasn't anybody
done that yet?

557
00:35:19.585 --> 00:35:23.220
Because they didn't have
the primordial sample.

558
00:35:25.056 --> 00:35:26.456
We do.

559
00:35:39.370 --> 00:35:41.371
Bridge. commo.
get me the captain.

560
00:35:46.210 --> 00:35:47.944
Sir. we finally
got the comms up.

561
00:35:47.946 --> 00:35:49.212
This came through.

562
00:35:49.214 --> 00:35:51.615
A message from potus.
This is five days old.

563
00:35:51.617 --> 00:35:53.350
Yes. sir. It was transmitted
while the radios were down.

564
00:35:53.352 --> 00:35:55.318
We need to confirm these orders.
Get me the pentagon.

565
00:35:55.320 --> 00:35:57.120
Sir. I've... I've been trying.
but there's no answer.

566
00:35:57.122 --> 00:36:01.024
I'll try the lab.
Get me the presidential bunker.

567
00:36:02.326 --> 00:36:03.727
North carolina's not safe.

568
00:36:03.729 --> 00:36:05.462
President wants us
to change course for mayport.

569
00:36:05.464 --> 00:36:07.497
There's a lab in jacksonville
that's supposed to be secure.

570
00:36:07.499 --> 00:36:09.366
There's no answer there
or the pentagon.

571
00:36:09.368 --> 00:36:12.369
Sir. nothing from the bunker.

572
00:36:12.371 --> 00:36:13.703
Maybe our signal's
not getting out.

573
00:36:13.705 --> 00:36:15.338
We check the transmit side?

574
00:36:15.340 --> 00:36:17.240
That's not the problem.
Their phones are ringing.

575
00:36:17.242 --> 00:36:19.776
Sir. I have another message
coming through!

576
00:36:21.512 --> 00:36:23.246
It was transmitted
at the same time as potus'.

577
00:36:23.248 --> 00:36:24.614
It looks like
a much bigger file.

578
00:36:26.617 --> 00:36:28.685
It's an mpeg. sir. Play it.

579
00:36:32.757 --> 00:36:34.257
<i>Tom.</i>

580
00:36:36.627 --> 00:36:38.261
<i>We're at your father's cabin.</i>

581
00:36:38.263 --> 00:36:39.663
<i>He thinks he has a way</i>
<i>to get this message out.</i>

582
00:36:39.665 --> 00:36:43.400
<i>Through his contacts</i>
<i>at the pentagon.</i>

583
00:36:43.402 --> 00:36:46.536
<i>I have no idea when you</i>
<i>might be seeing this.</i>

584
00:36:46.538 --> 00:36:50.273
<i>Or where you are.</i>

585
00:36:50.275 --> 00:36:52.375
<i>We're all healthy.</i>

586
00:36:52.377 --> 00:36:55.278
<i>We managed to get out early.</i>

587
00:36:55.280 --> 00:36:57.581
<i>And have been up here</i>
<i>for a couple months already.</i>

588
00:36:57.583 --> 00:37:03.286
<i>We haven't heard anything</i>
<i>from your brother or sister.</i>

589
00:37:03.288 --> 00:37:04.554
<i>For a while.</i>

590
00:37:04.556 --> 00:37:06.590
<i>My. um...</i>

591
00:37:08.693 --> 00:37:10.560
<i>My sister didn't make it.</i>

592
00:37:10.562 --> 00:37:15.165
<i>But. honey. we're fine.</i>

593
00:37:15.167 --> 00:37:17.667
<i>We really are.</i>

594
00:37:17.669 --> 00:37:22.439
<i>And I really hope</i>
<i>that you are. too.</i>

595
00:37:22.441 --> 00:37:24.608
<i>Kids!</i>

596
00:37:24.610 --> 00:37:26.243
<i>Come on out here.</i>

597
00:37:26.245 --> 00:37:27.811
<i>It's a tape for dad.</i>

598
00:37:27.813 --> 00:37:30.580
<i>Come on. Come. Come say hi.</i>

599
00:37:34.485 --> 00:37:37.187
<i>Daddy. where are you?</i>

600
00:37:37.189 --> 00:37:39.089
<i>We miss you.</i>

601
00:37:39.091 --> 00:37:41.758
Sam: <i>We love you. daddy.</i>

602
00:37:41.760 --> 00:37:45.428
<i>Just get here if you can.</i>

603
00:37:45.430 --> 00:37:48.465
<i>We love you so much.</i>

604
00:37:48.467 --> 00:37:51.468
<i>Okay. All right.</i>

605
00:37:51.470 --> 00:37:53.703
<i>Let's turn it off.</i>

606
00:38:09.487 --> 00:38:11.421
Hey.

607
00:38:13.224 --> 00:38:16.793
I don't know
what we're going home to.

608
00:38:23.367 --> 00:38:27.237
No radiation detected
within a 100-mile radius. sir.

609
00:38:27.239 --> 00:38:31.141
If america was nuked.
it wasn't here.

610
00:38:31.143 --> 00:38:33.877
We're home.

611
00:38:53.364 --> 00:38:56.366
You said you have what it takes
to make the vaccine.

612
00:38:56.368 --> 00:38:58.802
If you had to. could you do it
here on the ship?

613
00:38:58.804 --> 00:39:02.572
The lab wasn't built for that.

614
00:39:02.574 --> 00:39:04.541
It's for collecting data.

615
00:39:04.543 --> 00:39:05.875
But if you had to. could you?

616
00:39:10.781 --> 00:39:12.749
The expeditionary team
will forward deploy.

617
00:39:12.751 --> 00:39:14.651
And secure the area
for the next group.

618
00:39:14.653 --> 00:39:16.419
Hopefully we'll find support.

619
00:39:16.421 --> 00:39:18.455
Got to be prepared for anything.

620
00:39:18.457 --> 00:39:21.458
Everyone carries
their own biohazard suit.

621
00:39:21.460 --> 00:39:24.394
We do not engage
unless we are engaged.

622
00:39:26.831 --> 00:39:29.933
Prepare your people
and await further orders.

623
00:39:29.935 --> 00:39:31.968
Dismissed.

624
00:39:41.579 --> 00:39:43.513
There's still no answer
from potus.

625
00:39:43.515 --> 00:39:45.548
And nothing from mayport
or the lab.

626
00:39:45.550 --> 00:39:47.617
We can't even get
an f.M. Radio signal.

627
00:39:47.619 --> 00:39:49.853
If the power grid's down.
that means everything's down.

628
00:39:49.855 --> 00:39:52.822
We'll know more when
we get boots on the ground.

629
00:39:52.824 --> 00:39:54.858
Mike. we're not going home.

630
00:39:54.860 --> 00:39:57.727
What are you talking about?

631
00:39:57.729 --> 00:40:00.330
The lab's 200 miles inland.

632
00:40:00.332 --> 00:40:02.332
You saw the news footage.

633
00:40:02.334 --> 00:40:03.867
We'll fight our way in there
if we have to.

634
00:40:03.869 --> 00:40:05.368
And then what?

635
00:40:05.370 --> 00:40:07.337
Generators run out
in a couple weeks.

636
00:40:07.339 --> 00:40:09.773
Maybe the civilian population
tries to overrun it.

637
00:40:09.775 --> 00:40:11.241
There's too many variables.

638
00:40:11.243 --> 00:40:12.876
So. what do we do?
We stay on the ship?

639
00:40:12.878 --> 00:40:15.211
Dr. Scott says she has what she
needs right here. Dr. Scott.

640
00:40:15.213 --> 00:40:16.546
We have standing orders.

641
00:40:16.548 --> 00:40:18.214
From the president
of the United States.

642
00:40:18.216 --> 00:40:19.749
From five days ago.

643
00:40:19.751 --> 00:40:21.751
In the absence
of a command structure.

644
00:40:21.753 --> 00:40:24.487
I decide what's in the best
interest of our mission.

645
00:40:24.489 --> 00:40:27.223
And we have enough food here
to last us what. a week?

646
00:40:27.225 --> 00:40:28.358
How much fuel?

647
00:40:28.360 --> 00:40:29.559
We'll find what we need.

648
00:40:29.561 --> 00:40:31.661
We'll die out there.
No. We will not.

649
00:40:31.663 --> 00:40:33.229
Tom. I appreciate
what you're trying to do.

650
00:40:33.231 --> 00:40:35.331
But it's not gonna work.
People want to get home.

651
00:40:35.333 --> 00:40:38.768
And who exactly gets to go home.

652
00:40:38.770 --> 00:40:43.907
When we have 80 biohazard suits
for 216 people?

653
00:40:46.677 --> 00:40:47.944
We draw lots.

654
00:40:47.946 --> 00:40:50.780
I can't think like that. mike.

655
00:40:50.782 --> 00:40:52.415
It'll at least
give people a chance.

656
00:40:52.417 --> 00:40:54.350
To get back to their families.
to say goodbye.

657
00:40:54.352 --> 00:40:56.786
I'm not letting anybody
on this ship give up.

658
00:40:56.788 --> 00:40:58.254
That's not your call.
You don't get to play god.

659
00:40:58.256 --> 00:41:01.024
I'm still the captain
of this ship.

660
00:41:01.026 --> 00:41:03.426
Now. I've laid out our mission.

661
00:41:03.428 --> 00:41:06.896
I expect you to fall in line.

662
00:41:16.774 --> 00:41:18.975
Rios: Captain's on the bridge.

663
00:41:30.554 --> 00:41:33.289
Left full rudder.
All engines ahead flank.

664
00:41:33.291 --> 00:41:34.591
Sir?

665
00:41:36.660 --> 00:41:38.528
Left full rudder.

666
00:41:38.530 --> 00:41:40.630
All engines ahead flank.

667
00:41:41.966 --> 00:41:44.534
Aye. aye. Left full rudder.

668
00:41:44.536 --> 00:41:45.935
All engines ahead flank.

669
00:41:45.937 --> 00:41:47.837
Left full rudder.
All engines ahead flank. aye.

670
00:42:07.558 --> 00:42:09.759
This is the captain speaking.

671
00:42:09.761 --> 00:42:12.729
<i>We have no contact with home.</i>

672
00:42:12.731 --> 00:42:14.631
<i>And I have good reason</i>
<i>to believe.</i>

673
00:42:14.633 --> 00:42:17.467
<i>That the american government</i>
<i>is no longer functioning.</i>

674
00:42:17.469 --> 00:42:20.904
The country we all hoped we were
coming back to no longer exists.

675
00:42:20.906 --> 00:42:23.406
<i>We left these shores</i>
<i>four months ago.</i>

676
00:42:23.408 --> 00:42:25.742
<i>As members</i>
<i>of the United States navy.</i>

677
00:42:25.744 --> 00:42:28.478
<i>But now we are more than that.</i>

678
00:42:28.480 --> 00:42:31.114
<i>Now our duty</i>
<i>is to the entire world.</i>

679
00:42:31.116 --> 00:42:35.952
On board this ship
is the hope...

680
00:42:35.954 --> 00:42:39.355
For our futures.
for our families.

681
00:42:39.357 --> 00:42:41.624
And for all of humanity.

682
00:42:41.626 --> 00:42:43.993
Because in that lab
in our helo bay.

683
00:42:43.995 --> 00:42:46.729
<i>Are the ingredients for a cure.</i>

684
00:42:46.731 --> 00:42:49.065
And this is the safest place
on earth.

685
00:42:49.067 --> 00:42:51.634
For our scientists
to do their work...

686
00:42:51.636 --> 00:42:54.070
<i>On a $3 billion</i>
<i>piece of machinery.</i>

687
00:42:54.072 --> 00:42:57.907
<i>Protected by 216 sailors</i>
<i>in the u.S. Navy.</i>

688
00:42:57.909 --> 00:43:01.010
Our mission now is simple.

689
00:43:01.012 --> 00:43:03.780
We do whatever it takes
to stay alive at sea.

690
00:43:03.782 --> 00:43:05.481
Until they find that cure.

691
00:43:05.483 --> 00:43:07.917
<i>There's an unmanned</i>
<i>food and fuel station.</i>

692
00:43:07.919 --> 00:43:09.485
<i>Outside guantanamo bay.</i>

693
00:43:09.487 --> 00:43:11.988
<i>For the moment.</i>
<i>that is our destination.</i>

694
00:43:15.893 --> 00:43:20.430
We've lost so much already.

695
00:43:20.432 --> 00:43:23.499
But this is the most courageous
and resilient crew.

696
00:43:23.501 --> 00:43:26.402
With whom I have ever
been privileged to serve.

697
00:43:26.404 --> 00:43:29.939
<i>We will come through this</i>
<i>together.</i>

698
00:43:29.941 --> 00:43:33.476
<i>And we will prevail.</i>

699
00:43:34.979 --> 00:43:36.646
Carry on.

700
00:43:52.096 --> 00:43:53.963
Attention on deck.

701
00:43:58.969 --> 00:44:01.004
Lieutenant granderson.

702
00:44:01.006 --> 00:44:02.972
Permission to salute
the captain.

703
00:44:02.974 --> 00:44:05.908
Permission granted.

704
00:44:07.778 --> 00:44:09.278
Hand salute!
